---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import HubNav from '../../../components/HubNav.astro';
import { BOOTNODES, TESTNET_RPC_URL } from '../../../config/testnet';
import '../../../styles/hub-common.css';

const REL = 'testnet-v0.1.14';
const relUrl = `https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network/releases/tag/${REL}`;
const boot = BOOTNODES.join(',');
const contactEmail = 'nico.builds@boing.network';
const discordUrl = 'https://discord.gg/K3w9nbUw4N';
const guideUrl = 'https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network/blob/main/docs/TESTNET-VALIDATOR-GUIDE.md';

const getBinary = `curl -sSLO https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network/releases/download/${REL}/release-linux-x86_64.zip
unzip release-linux-x86_64.zip && mv boing-node-linux-x86_64 boing-node && mv boing-linux-x86_64 boing && chmod +x boing-node boing
./boing validator --help`;
const getSource = `# Ubuntu / WSL: sudo apt install -y build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev clang git; Rust via https://rustup.rs
git clone https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network && cd boing.network
cargo build --release -p boing-node -p boing-cli
cp target/release/boing-node target/release/boing .`;
const consensusEnv = `BOING_CHAIN_ID=6913 BOING_VALIDATOR_SET=open BOING_OPEN_VALIDATOR_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=400 BOING_NAME_REGISTRY_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=640`;
const flyNotes = `cp fly.testnet-2.toml fly.toml      # set app = "<your-app>", drop the public RPC/CORS extras
# [env] keep BOING_CHAIN_ID / BOING_NAME_REGISTRY_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT, add:
#   BOING_VALIDATOR_SET = "open"   BOING_OPEN_VALIDATOR_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT = "400"
#   BOING_VALIDATOR = "1"          BOING_BOOTNODES = "${boot}"
fly volumes create boing_data --size 10
fly secrets set BOING_VALIDATOR_KEY="$(cat node.key)"   # from a chmod 600 file, never committed
fly deploy --remote-only`;
const unjail = `boing validator status --node <node id> --rpc-url ${TESTNET_RPC_URL}
# after the 500-block cooldown (owner key via env only, dry run first):
boing validator unjail --dry-run --rpc-url ${TESTNET_RPC_URL}
boing validator unjail --rpc-url ${TESTNET_RPC_URL}`;
const getDocker = `git clone https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network && cd boing.network
docker build -t boing-node .`;
const syncBinary = `export ${consensusEnv}
./boing-node \\
  --data-dir ./boing-data \\
  --p2p-listen /ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/4001 \\
  --bootnodes ${boot} \\
  --rpc-port 8545`;
const syncDocker = `docker run -d --name boing-node --restart unless-stopped \\
  -p 4001:4001 -p 127.0.0.1:8545:8545 \\
  -v boing-data:/data \\
  -e BOING_CHAIN_ID=6913 -e BOING_VALIDATOR_SET=open -e BOING_OPEN_VALIDATOR_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=400 \\
  -e BOING_NAME_REGISTRY_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=640 \\
  -e BOING_BOOTNODES=${boot} \\
  boing-node`;
const runValidator = `# validator.env  (chmod 600; never commit or share)
BOING_CHAIN_ID=6913
BOING_VALIDATOR_SET=open
BOING_OPEN_VALIDATOR_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=400
BOING_NAME_REGISTRY_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=640
BOING_VALIDATOR_KEY=<32-byte node key hex>

set -a; . ./validator.env; set +a
./boing-node --validator --data-dir ./boing-data \\
  --p2p-listen /ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/4001 \\
  --bootnodes ${boot} \\
  --rpc-port 8545`;
const monitor = `curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8545/live
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8545 -H 'content-type: application/json' \\
  -d '{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"boing_health","params":[]}'`;
---

<Layout
  title="Run a validator · Operator Hub · Testnet Portal"
  description="How to run a Boing Network testnet validator: open registration with a 100 BOING bond, hardware, node setup, keys, bootnodes, uptime, monitoring and duties."
>
  <article class="portal-page role-hub operators-hub hub-page hub-operator validator-guide" data-hub="node_operator">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Testnet Portal', href: '/testnet' }, { label: 'Operator Hub', href: '/testnet/operators' }, { label: 'Run a validator' }]} />
    <div class="hub-page-main">
    <HubNav hub="operator" current="validator" />
    <section class="section fade-in-up">
      <h1>Run a testnet validator</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Public testnet: chain <strong>6913</strong> (<code>0x1b01</code>), RPC <code>{TESTNET_RPC_URL}</code>,
        explorer <a href="https://boing.observer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">boing.observer</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="vg-note">
        <strong>How to become a validator today: open registration.</strong> Anyone can join: run a synced node, then
        <strong>register it with a 100 BOING bond</strong> (Boing Express → <strong>Validate</strong> tab, or
        <code>boing validator register</code>). You join the set at the next epoch (every 100 blocks) and must
        <strong>stay online</strong>: missing more than 10% of your scheduled proposals jails you (bond kept; unjail after a
        cooldown). No operator approval and no 10,000 BOING stake are needed. Details in
        <a href="#open-registration">Open validator registration</a>.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="hardware">
      <h2>1. Hardware and network</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Minimum:</strong> 2 vCPU (x86_64 or arm64), 2 GB RAM, 10 GB SSD.</li>
        <li><strong>Recommended:</strong> 4 vCPU, 4 GB RAM, 50 GB SSD, static public IPv4.</li>
        <li>Inbound <strong>TCP 4001</strong> (P2P) must be reachable. RPC 8545 only needs to be public if you serve RPC to others.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="node">
      <h2>2. Get the node</h2>
      <p><strong>Release binaries (recommended):</strong> download <a href={relUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{REL}</a> or newer (macOS and Windows zips are on the same page). The zip holds <code>boing-node-&lt;platform&gt;</code> and <code>boing-&lt;platform&gt;</code>, so rename them; there is no <code>--version</code> flag. Older releases lack open validator mode and fresh-node sync.</p>
      <pre><code>{getBinary}</code></pre>
      <p><strong>Build from source</strong> (alternative):</p>
      <pre><code>{getSource}</code></pre>
      <p><strong>Docker</strong> (build from source):</p>
      <pre><code>{getDocker}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="keys">
      <h2>3. Keys</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open <a href="https://boing.express" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Express</a> and <strong>Create wallet</strong> (or import a key) on Boing Testnet. Use a dedicated key for the validator.</li>
        <li>This wallet is the validator <strong>owner</strong>: it pays and holds the 100 BOING bond and signs register / deregister / unjail / claim.</li>
        <li>Create a separate <strong>node key</strong> (<code>BOING_VALIDATOR_KEY</code>, 32-byte hex): use <strong>Generate a new node key</strong> in the Validate tab (generated locally, never sent anywhere). Keep it in a file only you can read; never paste it into chat, a repo or shell history.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="stake">
      <h2>4. Fund the bond</h2>
      <p>Registering locks a <strong>100 BOING</strong> bond; keep a few BOING extra for fees (about 1 BOING per transaction). The <a href="/faucet">faucet</a> sends 20 BOING per request, once a minute, so a few requests cover the bond. Stuck or want help? Reach out with your <strong>AccountId</strong> and node multiaddr (<code>/ip4/&lt;public-ip&gt;/tcp/4001</code>):</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}?subject=Boing%20testnet%20validator%20stake%20request`}>{contactEmail}</a></li>
        <li>Discord: <a href={discordUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{discordUrl}</a> (operators channel)</li>
        <li>Also <a href="/testnet/register/operator">register as an operator</a> so your node shows on the leaderboard.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="sync">
      <h2>5. Sync from the testnet bootnodes</h2>
      <p>Official bootnodes (see <a href="/bootnodes">Bootnodes</a>):</p>
      <pre><code>{BOOTNODES.join('\n')}</code></pre>
      <p><strong>Binary:</strong></p>
      <pre><code>{syncBinary}</code></pre>
      <p><strong>Docker:</strong></p>
      <pre><code>{syncDocker}</code></pre>
      <p>Your node is synced when <code>boing_health</code> reports the same <code>head_height</code> as the public RPC.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="bond">
      <h2>6. Register</h2>
      <p>From <strong>Boing Express → Validate</strong> with the owner wallet (or <code>boing validator register --node-key-hex &lt;node key&gt;</code>):</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Unlock the owner wallet on Boing Testnet and open the <strong>Validate</strong> tab.</li>
        <li>Paste your node key (or generate one), check the node id, then <strong>Register validator (100 BOING bond)</strong>.</li>
        <li>Your validator shows as <strong>pending</strong> and joins at the next epoch. The tab shows its status, uptime, missed blocks, bond and jail stats.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>To leave: <strong>Deregister</strong>; the bond unlocks after about 100 blocks, then <strong>Claim unbond</strong>. Jailed? <strong>Unjail</strong> after the cooldown.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="validate">
      <h2>7. Run as a validator</h2>
      <p>Run with the validator flags and the open-mode settings used by the public nodes (key in an env file, not on the command line). Have it synced and running before your registration's epoch boundary:</p>
      <pre><code>{runValidator}</code></pre>
      <p>Docker: add <code>--env-file validator.env -e BOING_VALIDATOR=1</code>.</p>
      <h3 id="fly">Fly.io</h3>
      <pre><code>{flyNotes}</code></pre>
      <h3 id="unjail">Unjail</h3>
      <p>Jailed for missing more than 10% of your scheduled proposals? Your bond is kept. Fix the node first, then:</p>
      <pre><code>{unjail}</code></pre>
      <p>No <code>--faucet-enable</code> or <code>--validators</code> needed: with <code>BOING_CHAIN_ID=6913</code> the node applies the testnet network preset (genesis allocations, historical fee rules, anchor validator) and replays from genesis with identical roots.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="monitoring">
      <h2>8. Monitoring</h2>
      <pre><code>{monitor}</code></pre>
      <p>Watch that <code>head_height</code> keeps pace with the public RPC, you have at least one peer, and disk has room. Run under a supervisor (systemd <code>Restart=always</code> or Docker <code>--restart unless-stopped</code>) and alert when <code>/live</code> fails.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="open-registration">
      <h2>Open validator registration</h2>
      <p><strong>Live on testnet since block 400.</strong> Run your node with <code>BOING_VALIDATOR_SET=open</code> and <code>BOING_OPEN_VALIDATOR_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT=400</code> (the same values as the public nodes), then register from the CLI or the boing.express <strong>Validate</strong> tab:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Register:</strong> <code>boing validator register --node-key-hex &lt;node seed&gt;</code> locks a <strong>100 BOING</strong> bond. Your node key signs a proof that binds it to your account. One validator per account.</li>
        <li><strong>Join:</strong> at the next epoch boundary (every 100 blocks), up to a capped set size, in deterministic order.</li>
        <li><strong>Liveness:</strong> miss more than 10% of your scheduled proposals over the last 1,000 produced blocks and you're jailed at the next boundary. Idle periods never count. Your bond is kept; after a cooldown run <code>boing validator unjail</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>Leave:</strong> <code>boing validator deregister</code>; the bond unlocks after 100 blocks (claim with <code>ClaimUnbond</code>).</li>
        <li><strong>Status:</strong> <code>boing validator status</code> or RPC <code>boing_getValidators</code>: status, uptime %, missed count and bond.</li>
        <li><strong>Anchors:</strong> the permanent bootstrap validators keep the chain producing even if every open validator is offline.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="stake-set">
      <h2>Future: stake-based validator set (not active)</h2>
      <p>The node also implements a stake-weighted mode that may be enabled later at an announced <strong>activation height</strong>. It is <strong>not active</strong>: today validators join through open registration (100 BOING bond, above). If it is ever enabled:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Joining:</strong> every 100 committed blocks (epoch boundary) all nodes recompute the set from chain state: accounts with at least <strong>10,000 BOING</strong> bonded, highest stake first (ties by AccountId), top <strong>21</strong>. Qualify and you join at the next boundary, so have your node synced and running with <code>BOING_VALIDATOR=1</code> before then.</li>
        <li><strong>Leaving:</strong> unbonding lowers active stake immediately; below 10,000 BOING (or outside the top 21) you leave at the next boundary.</li>
        <li><strong>Deterministic and persistent:</strong> every node derives the same set; it is saved as <code>stake_validator_set.json</code> in the data directory and restored on restart.</li>
        <li><strong>Bootstrap fallback:</strong> if nobody qualifies, the static bootstrap list is used, so the chain never runs with an empty set.</li>
        <li><strong>Flags</strong> (identical on all nodes): <code>BOING_VALIDATOR_SET=stake</code> and <code>BOING_STAKE_VALIDATOR_ACTIVATION_HEIGHT</code>. Wait for the announcement; don't enable stake mode early.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Stopping? Keep your node online until the boundary after your unbond has removed you.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="duties">
      <h2>9. Duties</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Keep the node online and in sync; missed rounds hurt the network and your leaderboard standing.</li>
        <li>Upgrade promptly when a new <code>testnet-v*</code> release is announced; consensus changes are coordinated in an announced window.</li>
        <li>Protect the validator key and report a suspected compromise immediately.</li>
        <li>Keep TCP 4001 reachable so other nodes can peer with you.</li>
        <li>This is a testnet: BOING has no monetary value and the chain may be reset.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="muted">Full guide in the repo: <a href={guideUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/TESTNET-VALIDATOR-GUIDE.md</a>.</p>
    </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .validator-guide pre {
    overflow-x: auto;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  .validator-guide .vg-note {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent-teal, #2dd4bf);
    background: rgba(45, 212, 191, 0.08);
    border-radius: 6px;
  }
  .validator-guide section h2 { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  .validator-guide ol, .validator-guide ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; }
</style>